# Manual test of the settlement flow. Runs in the IntelliJ HTTP Client and in the VS Code / Cursor REST Client.
# Start the app first (see README). Run the requests from top to bottom: the expected results assume
# a fresh start with the seeded bets.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Pending bets of EVT-1001 (bets 1 and 3 picked TEAM-RMA, bet 2 picked TEAM-FCB)
GET {{host}}/api/bets?eventId=EVT-1001

### 2. One bet
GET {{host}}/api/bets/1

### 3. Publish the outcome of EVT-1001: Real Madrid wins. Expect 202 Accepted.
POST {{host}}/api/event-outcomes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EVT-1001",
  "eventName": "Real Madrid vs Barcelona",
  "eventWinnerId": "TEAM-RMA"
}

### 4. Bets of EVT-1001 after settlement: bets 1 and 3 WON, bet 2 LOST, each with settledAt
# Settlement is asynchronous. If the bets are still PENDING, wait a second and run again.
GET {{host}}/api/bets?eventId=EVT-1001

### 5. Pending bets: only the two bets of EVT-2002 are left (after step 4 shows the settled bets)
GET {{host}}/api/bets?status=PENDING

### 6. Place a bet on a new event. Expect 201 Created with a Location header.
POST {{host}}/api/bets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "user-9",
  "eventId": "EVT-3003",
  "eventMarketId": "MKT-MATCH-WINNER",
  "eventWinnerId": "TEAM-Z",
  "amount": 12.50
}

### 7. Publish the outcome of EVT-3003: TEAM-Z wins. Expect 202 Accepted.
POST {{host}}/api/event-outcomes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EVT-3003",
  "eventName": "Team Z vs Team Y",
  "eventWinnerId": "TEAM-Z"
}

### 8. The new bet is WON. If it is still PENDING, wait a second and run again.
GET {{host}}/api/bets?eventId=EVT-3003

### 9. Error: outcome without a winner. Expect 400 with errors.eventWinnerId.
POST {{host}}/api/event-outcomes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EVT-1001",
  "eventName": "Real Madrid vs Barcelona"
}

### 10. Error: unknown bet. Expect 404.
GET {{host}}/api/bets/999

### 11. Error: unknown status value. Expect 400.
GET {{host}}/api/bets?status=OPEN

### 12. Error: negative amount. Expect 400 with errors.amount.
POST {{host}}/api/bets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "user-9",
  "eventId": "EVT-3003",
  "eventMarketId": "MKT-MATCH-WINNER",
  "eventWinnerId": "TEAM-Z",
  "amount": -5
}
